      "table_ref": "Table 1",
      "description": "Summary statistics (means over 34 years of annual means, SDs, medians, skewness, min/max annual means) for ILLIQ, SIZE, DIVYLD, SDRET; NYSE stocks, 1963-1996.",
      "replication_meaning": "Proves correct universe construction (NYSE common stocks with the paper's four admission criteria: >200 days of return/volume data in year y-1, listed at year-end y-1, price > $5 at year-end y-1, ILLIQ outside the 1% tails excluded) and correct variable construction — ILLIQ per eq. (1) with the x10^6 scaling, CRSP market cap SIZE, dividend yield, and daily-return SDRET — over the 1963-1996 characteristic years, using the paper's annual-statistics-then-average convention. Matching these distributions validates the admitted sample before any regression is run.",
      "paper_quote": "Stocks admitted in each year $y$ have more than 200 days of data for the calculation of the characteristics and their end-of-year price exceeds $5. Excluded are stocks whose $ ILLIQ_{iy} $ is at the extreme 1% upper and lower tails of the distribution.",
