      "replication_meaning": "Proves the Fama-MacBeth machinery end-to-end: 408 monthly cross-sections of delisting-adjusted returns (Shumway -30% imputation for codes 500/520/551-573/574/580/584) on year y-1 characteristics, the mean-adjusted ILLIQMA signal (eq. 4), Scholes-Williams size-portfolio betas, and the time-series averaging with t-tests — including the January-exclusion and two 17-year subperiod breakdowns. The headline k_ILLIQMA = 0.162 (t = 6.55) confirms illiquidity is priced in the cross-section and that the lag structure (characteristics from y-1, returns in y) is correct.",
      "paper_quote": "The data include 408 months over 34 years, 1964–1997, (the stock characteristics are calculated for the years 1963–1996).",
